// DodgeBot: a human-like dodge brain for Lab > Targets strafers.
//
// The stock strafe brains are open-loop: they roll random legs and never look
// at the player. This brain closes the loop. Every 0.05 s it reads what a real
// opponent would read off you:
//   - where your crosshair is relative to its body, and whether it is closing in
//   - shots you fire that pass near it (server weapon-attack callback)
//   - damage it takes
// and answers after a human reaction delay with what Apex players actually do:
// strafe combos built from short taps and long commits (long strafe, short ->
// long, short-short -> long bait, ADAD -> commit, long -> long swing), a hurt
// retreat, and range control around where it spawned. It never crouches: real
// players do not crouch-strafe in a gunfight, so the Lab crouch row is ignored.
//
// It takes over any strafer the stock Lab spawns (Add Strafer, the strafer
// challenge, manual slots), dummy or legend body. A legend body is driven like a
// human (stick input + view angles) and shoots back on DodgeBot's own fire and
// aim settings, whatever the Lab target preset is. Lab speed slider, strafing
// off, god mode and armor still apply.
//
// Console (per player): dodgebot          -> show level
//                       dodgebot 0        -> off, stock brain back
//                       dodgebot 1|2|3    -> casual | ranked | pro
//                       dodgebot speed unarmed|hipfire|ads|off|<50-400>
//                         -> 199 | 173 | 130 u/s | Lab slider | custom
//                       dodgebot respawn on|off|<min m> <max m>
//                         -> after a kill, respawn 10-17 m around you, any direction
//                       dodgebot fire on|off      -> legend bots shoot back (default on)
//                       dodgebot ads off|auto|on  -> legend bots aim down sights (default auto)
//                       dodgebot aim <0-100>      -> legend bot aim (default 50)

global function CodeCallback_Trainer_DodgeBot_ModInit
